  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "A square of side length 2 is drawn. A second square is formed when the midpoints of the first square are joined. A third square is formed when the midpoints of the second square are joined, and so on. Find the total area of all the squares formed in this way.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$8$ square units.",
      "worked": "Joining the midpoints forms a square with half the area of the preceding square. The areas therefore form a geometric series with first term $4$ and common ratio $\\frac12$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}S&=4+2+1+\\frac12+\\cdots\\\\S&=\\frac{4}{1-\\frac12}\\\\S&=8.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe total area is $8$ square units.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 43
  },
